  {
    "id": "selectSite",
    "type": "click",
    "teaches": "The Markov blanket of a site: a state variable is conditionally independent of the whole field given its four lattice neighbors and its own observation."
  },
  {
    "id": "modelLayers",
    "type": "toggle",
    "label": "Model view",
    "options": [
      "Hidden lattice only",
      "Observation links only",
      "Full model"
    ],
    "default": "Full model",
    "teaches": "That the model factorizes into two distinct pieces — neighbor-to-neighbor coupling among hidden states, and one per-site evidence attachment from each observation."
  },
  {
    "id": "coupling",
    "type": "slider",
    "label": "Pairwise coupling strength β",
    "range": [
      0,
      1,
      0.01
    ],
    "default": 0,
    "teaches": "Stronger pairwise potentials drive neighboring hidden states toward equal values, producing spatial smoothness, while the observations stay fixed."
  }
]

DEMO STEPS (tween through these using goToStep(); each step drives the controls above):
[
  {
    "title": "Hidden state lattice",
    "narration": "Only the white x nodes and their grid edges are shown: each site is joined to its four lattice neighbors, and the edges run off frame to signal an unbounded array.",
